# Git — user control

The maintainer is the only one who commits and pushes in this repository.

Do **not** run `git commit`, create merge commits, `git push`, or destructive git history
commands unless the user explicitly requests that exact operation in the current message.

Allowed without an explicit commit/push request: `git fetch`, merge (may leave repo merging),
conflict resolution, file edits, tests, `git add`, and reporting `git status` / `git diff` for review.

After git-heavy work, do not commit — tell the user what to review before they commit or push.
